        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-12T15:34:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alright, I think we should plan on moving Skia towards 2), where all local matrix control is encapsulated within SkLocalMatrixShader. I looked briefly into doing this today and it ends up being a pretty invasive change given how integrated SkShaderBase\u0027s local matrix field is with raster pipeline, context, SkVM, and FP creation is. I think 2) will let a lot of this logic become much simpler.\n\nFor the time being, I think Graphite should move forward as if 2) will happen soon, and not worry too much about paint keys that have a local matrix block followed by an image shader that also, temporarily, adds its own local matrix block.  We can easily delete that second block once images/gradients/runtime effects don\u0027t have a local matrix. For now, we can just update our check on their addToKey() implementations to only add the local matrix block if their transform is not identity.",
      "parentUuid": "ab42c31c_49deae63",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1226,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1226,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "94c2d46725b50f3e174be72e740fa2f1378d889b",
